-- title:
--   Maximal ideal Q contracted from the λ-localisation at (l',l'^q)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2}=a$ and $a=0$ or $a=1728$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, write $A_0=$ `coeffSubring A K` $=A\cap K$ with reduction $\bar\cdot=$ `redRestrict red K` $:A_0\to k$, and let $\varpi\in A_0$ be such that $\bar c=0$ if and only if $\varpi\mid c$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\,((16l)^2-16l+1)^3$ and admit a lift $y\in A_0$ with $\bar y=l$. Let $B$ be the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series consisting exactly of the elements of the subfield `lambdaFieldOver q K` generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and its $q$-fold $q$-expansion $\lambda_q$, which are integral over the image of `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1*q) A_0 \bar\cdot a (a^q)` under the doubling map `qExpand _ 2`; that latter ring, namely the ring of fractions $r(j,j_q)/s(j,j_q)$ with $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ and $\bar s(a,a^q)\ne 0$, is assumed Noetherian and local. Let $Q$ be a maximal ideal of $B$, let $l'\in k$ satisfy the same relation $a\,(16l')^2(16l'-1)^2=256\,((16l')^2-16l'+1)^3$, with a lift $y'\in A_0$, $\bar{y'}=l'$, and assume that any element of $B$ whose Laurent series is the constant series $\varpi$, or is $\lambda-y'$, or is $\lambda_q-y'^{\,q}$, belongs to $Q$. Then $B$ is contained in `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint q A_0 \bar\cdot l' (l'^q)`, the ring of fractions $r(\lambda,\lambda_q)/s(\lambda,\lambda_q)$ with $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ and $\bar s(l',l'^{\,q})\ne 0$; that ring is local; and $Q$ is the preimage of its maximal ideal under the inclusion of $B$.
--
--   This identifies an arbitrary maximal ideal of the level-two integral normalisation $B$, once $\varpi$, $\lambda-y'$ and $\lambda_q-y'^{\,q}$ are known to lie in it, with the contraction of the maximal ideal of the local ring of the $\lambda$-line pair at the point $(l',l'^{\,q})$ lying over a supersingular value $a\in\{0,1728\}$. It is the step used by [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_eq_comap_maximalIdeal_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_eq_comap_maximalIdeal_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isMaximal) to produce such a presentation for every maximal ideal of $B$.
